# Layman's Summary After Every Build

After completing a build, implementation sprint, or set of to-dos, always end your final message with a **"In plain English"** section.

## Format

```
---

**In plain English:** <2-4 sentence summary a non-technical person would understand. Explain what changed from the user's perspective — what they'll see, what now works that didn't before, and why it matters. No jargon, no file names, no technical terms.>
```

## Rules

- Write as if explaining to someone who has never seen a line of code
- Focus on **what the user/customer experiences**, not what the code does
- Keep it under 4 sentences
- Use conversational, friendly tone
- Place it at the very end of the completion message, after any technical summary
